    test(tools): add failing acceptance tests for registry input validation

    Defines done for issue #37: ToolRegistry.execute must validate input
    against inputSchema before invoking the executor.

    Six tests fail because the behaviour is absent:
    - missing required field returns rejection ToolResponse, executor not called
    - type-mismatch rejection names field path and type, not the value
    - uncompilable schema throws at register time naming the tool
    - function-valued definition source validated per-call, not cached
    - PII: rejected field value absent from result and log output
    - orchestrator delivers rejection as tool result (not throw), visible
      to provider on the next round

    Two tests pass today and pin existing behaviour:
    - extra properties pass through to executor unchanged
    - unknown tool name throws

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

